## Work tracking (beads)

This project uses bd (beads). Run `bd prime` for commands; `docs/PROCESS.md` is the policy.
These rules override general guidance:

- Session start: report in_progress + ready before acting. in_progress beats ready.
- Claim before editing. One claimed bead per session. Run `bops lint <id>` first; if `workable` is false, fix the bead or pick another — do not claim anyway. Then `bops claim <id>`, which exits 3 on `lost` or `refused`, so pick another bead. Raw `bd update --claim` bypasses the claim lock.
- Session protocol: `bops next` → create a worktree for the bead → `bops claim <id>` inside it → work → `bops note <id>` at each milestone and at least hourly → push and open the PR → `bops land <id> --ref <pr-url> --sha <sha> --verify` → `bops release <id> --reason done` → `bops sync`. `bops land` never merges or closes; `bops sweep --dry-run=false` closes beads whose PRs have merged. If review asks for changes after release, `bops claim --resume <id>` takes the bead back. The `bops` skill has the full loop.
- Notes use `COMPLETED / IN PROGRESS / NEXT / BLOCKER / KEY DECISION`. `NEXT` is one concrete step a stranger could execute.
- File discovered work immediately: `bd create "..." --deps discovered-from:<current-id>`. Decide blocker-or-defer; move on.
- Only `blocks` for hard prerequisites. Validate with `bd blocked`. Name beads by WHAT, never "Phase N".
- Irreversible or money-spending actions: `bd gate create --type human --blocks <id> --reason "..."`, label `needs-human`, stop.
- Close only when every acceptance criterion is verified; cite the verification in `--reason`. Never close epics. Never resolve a human gate.
- Before stopping or when context is getting long: write the handoff note, then `bd sync` if online.
- Never create markdown TODO/PLAN files. Never `bd import issues.jsonl` as sync. Never `export BEADS_DIR`.
